From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] cuda/hip: fold the GDN beta/alpha elementwise chains into the grouped-mmvf epilogue (+3.4% decode)

Round-13 decode profile (rocprofv3, 34 tokens, verified r12 build, confirmed
identical in shape under llama-server): 6.03 ms of kernel per token spread over
~1085 dispatches, of which roughly 500 are elementwise kernels moving 32 to
4096 floats. Each costs 1.2-1.7 us of GPU time plus ~1.5 us of graph-replay
overhead for work that fits in one lane's registers.

The densest cluster is the GDN gating prologue. Every one of the 30 linear
layers runs, right after the grouped beta/alpha matvec:

    beta  = sigmoid(ssm_beta @ x)                      1.28 us
    tmp   = (ssm_alpha @ x) + ssm_dt                   1.60 us
    gate  = softplus(tmp) * ssm_a                      1.47 us   (0012 fusion)

Three launches over 32 floats each. 0022 already had the machinery to apply a
sigmoid in the grouped-mmvf segment epilogue, but it matched only a sigmoid
whose src IS the segment output, so it caught the shared-expert gate and never
beta - which reaches its matvec through a ggml_reshape view. This patch:

1. `mmvf.cu/.cuh`: the segment epilogue gains a second form,
   `softplus(sum + bias[row]) * scale[row]`, evaluated as the same three f32
   statements in the same order as the ADD / op_softplus / MUL kernels it
   replaces, on the same accumulator value those kernels would have loaded.
   Per-segment `bias` / `scale` pointers carry ssm_dt and ssm_a.
2. `ggml-cuda.cu`: the matcher walks whole-tensor alias links (reshape/view,
   equal element count, zero offset, single consumer at every step) back to the
   segment, and recognises the ADD -> SOFTPLUS -> MUL chain as well as the bare
   sigmoid. -90 launches and ~129 us of kernel per decoded token.
3. `qwen35moe.cpp`: the beta/alpha matvecs and both chains are emitted BEFORE
   the qkv/z projections, and each chain is pinned with
   ggml_build_forward_expand. Ops, operands and shapes are unchanged; only the
   position in the node list moves.

(3) is not cosmetic - it is most of the win. The hoisted epilogue write has to
be legal at group-launch time, and the graph allocator was handing these
128-byte results the buffers of tensors that were still being read: with the
chains emitted after the conv block, `gate` landed inside the 128 KB conv-input
concat, and `beta_sigmoid` landed on the attn_norm activation that the group
kernel itself reads. Both are genuine races, correctly declined. Emitting the
chains while `cur` is still live removes the aliasing, and coverage goes from
0/30 layers to 30/30 (+2.1% -> +3.4%).

Two matcher rules were needed to stop the two folds blocking each other:
the intermediate-hazard scan now exempts group members' own matvec
destinations (a folded member never materialises its matvec dst; the member
loop compares EFFECTIVE destinations instead), and it exempts nodes another
accepted fold has already absorbed (their reads happen from registers, or not
at all). The scan runs three passes so a fold accepted late unblocks one
rejected early. `GGML_CUDA_MMVF_EPI_DEBUG=1` prints every accept/decline with
the offending pointer pair - the allocation-dependent declines are impossible
to reason about from source alone.

Measured (runner box, R9700, HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0):

- same-binary toggle A/B (GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_MMVF_EPI_EXT=1 restores the
  pre-patch direct-src-sigmoid-only matcher), 3 rounds:
  tg128 132.91-133.06 off -> 137.28-137.50 on (**+3.35%**, 3/3 disjoint);
  pp512 neutral (4142-4191 off vs 4158-4186 on)
- an earlier build without the (3) reorder measured +2.13% over 5/5 disjoint
  rounds - the reorder is worth the other +1.2%
- whole-process stock vs cand, 5 rounds: tg128 80.50-81.16 -> 137.15-137.46
  (ratio 1.694), pp512 3183-3231 -> 4125-4156 (ratio 1.298)
- decode dispatch trace: the 30x sigmoid(32), 30x add(32) and 30x
  softplus-mul(32) launches per token are gone
- ppl on the runner corpus, 3 loads: see README (band 0.5% vs stock 3.9314)
- test-backend-ops MUL_MAT / ADD / MUL / UNARY / SSM_CONV / GATED_DELTA_NET OK
- llama-server smoke: coherent short, long and concurrent completions

Arithmetic note: the folded expressions are the stock statements on the stock
accumulator value, so the fold itself is exact. The node reordering in (3) does
change which OTHER allocation-dependent fusions fire around the GDN block, so
this ships as the same ppl-gated equivalence class as 0024/0026/0028/0031
rather than as a byte-identity claim.
